  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **POS Tagging** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef nlp_pos_tagging(train_tokens: list, train_tags: list, test_tokens: list, fallback_tag: str = 'NOUN') -> list:\n    c = {}\n    for tok, tag in zip(train_tokens, train_tags):\n        w = tok.lower(); c.setdefault(w, {})[tag] = c.setdefault(w, {}).get(tag, 0) + 1\n    return [max(c[t.lower()], key=c[t.lower()].get) if t.lower() in c else fallback_tag for t in test_tokens]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
